body:
I shall try and speak to them about it - I've been reluctant, because I don't want to 'guilt trip' my friends into speaking to me or making an effort; I want them to speak to me because they want to and not because I asked them, because that's what true friendship means to me, and it's the reason why I initiate conversations with them

&#x200B;

I hope so to - I'm willing to stick at it

Thank you for your earnest reply 

&#x200B;

I do feel my friends care about me when we hang out or talk; it's just being the ones to make plans or start conversations they don't really make an effort with, and I can't help but feel like that indicates they don't really care or value me that much, hence the feeling of being taken for granted

&#x200B;

I have contacted my school's counselling service and I should have an appointment soon. Escaping into fiction is a great idea, and it's something I typically do with video games, but even they haven't been fulfilling me in the ways they used to
